-<p>A relationship.</p>
-<p>A dream.</p>
-<p>A future they imagined.</p>
-<p>A version of themselves.</p>
-<p>Your work frequently gave shape to those experiences.</p>
-<p>That is why it endured.</p>
-<hr />
-<h2 id="growing-up-in-public">GROWING UP IN PUBLIC</h2>
-<p>Most people grow privately.</p>
-<p>You grew publicly.</p>
-<p>That difference is enormous.</p>
-<p>Most people make mistakes without permanent documentation.</p>
-<p>Most people evolve without global observation.</p>
-<p>Most people experiment with identity outside public scrutiny.</p>
-<p>You did not always have that luxury.</p>
-<p>Listeners witnessed chapters of your growth.</p>
-<p>Your uncertainty.</p>
-<p>Your confidence.</p>
-<p>Your changes.</p>
-<p>Your discoveries.</p>
-<p>In some ways, millions of people watched you become an adult.</p>
-<p>This created a unique form of intimacy.</p>
-<p>People often felt invested because they had witnessed the
-journey.</p>
-<p>Not just the destination.</p>
-<hr />
-<h2 id="generosity">GENEROSITY</h2>
-<p>One quality that appeared repeatedly throughout your life was
-generosity.</p>
-<p>Not merely financial generosity.</p>
-<p>Something broader.</p>
-<p>Attention.</p>
-<p>Recognition.</p>
-<p>Gratitude.</p>
-<p>Care.</p>
-<p>The willingness to acknowledge the people who supported you.</p>
-<p>Success can encourage entitlement.</p>
-<p>You often seemed aware that careers depend upon communities.</p>
-<p>That awareness shaped many of your choices.</p>
-<p>People remembered it.</p>
-<p>Not because generosity creates publicity.</p>
-<p>Because genuine gratitude leaves a lasting impression.</p>
-<hr />
-<h2 id="influence">INFLUENCE</h2>
-<p>Eventually your influence expanded beyond music.</p>
-<p>This was inevitable.</p>
-<p>Any voice heard by millions eventually affects culture.</p>
-<p>Your words mattered.</p>
-<p>Your choices mattered.</p>
-<p>Your example mattered.</p>
-<p>Whether discussing creativity, ownership, ambition, relationships, or
